# License scopes

The KLStream engine under `source/` retains the GNU Affero General Public License,
version 3, from the legacy project. See `source/LICENSE` for the complete license.
The original legacy README's MIT claim was inconsistent with its actual license
and is not carried forward.

Software Factory code, specifications, templates and tests under `factory/` retain
the author's proprietary license, preserved verbatim in `factory/LICENSE`.
The supplied factory bootstrap and associated root documentation under `docs/`
(COVERAGE, FORENSIC_AUDIT, MIGRATION, REFERENCES, RELEASE_SCOPE, SCHEMA, VALIDATION,
audit_tools and v26_forensic_results) retain those same supplied terms.
Including those files in this repository does not grant an additional license.

Research planning and audit documents are supplied by the project author with no
new general-purpose license grant in this migration. Third-party datasets keep
their own terms; public availability does not establish redistribution permission.
The author should choose and document a license for new research artifacts before
an artifact submission. This file records scope; it does not relicense prior work.
